===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To get mud on (something).
#: {{ux|en|If you '''muddy''' your shoes don’t wear them inside.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make a [[mess]] of, or create [[confusion]] with regard to; to [[muddle]].
#: {{ux|en|The discussion only '''muddied''' their understanding of the subject.}}
#* '''2014''', Steve Rose, "[http://www.theguardian.com/film/2014/jul/01/dawn-of-the-planet-of-the-apes-review Dawn of the Planet of the Apes: a primate scream - first look review]", ''The Guardian'', 1 July 2014:
#*: As the humans establish tentative bonds with their evolutionary cousins, the inter-species waters start to '''muddy'''.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Alex McLevy|title=''[[w:Game of Thrones|Game Of Thrones]]'' Suffers the Fog of War in the Battle against the Dead (Newbies)|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210531120501/https://www.avclub.com/game-of-thrones-suffers-the-fog-of-war-in-the-battle-ag-1834367999|archivedate=31 May 2021|work={{w|The A.V. Club}}|date=28 April 2019|passage=It may have been effective at conveying the confusion of the situation, but it didn’t make for terribly thrilling scenes. The blurry camerawork (quite literally at times) and rapid-fire editing meant that exchanges of blows that should have been viscerally thrilling were often '''muddied''', good for capturing the mood but not much fun to watch.}}

